/Risk-surviving Sailor.webp","rank":"Normal","race":null,"movement":"Ground","attackPosition":"Melee","damageType":["Physical"],"flavourText":"Sailing in the Salt Flat is a hazardous affair to begin with, but some sailors seek even greater thrills, such as hanging from a flying fin, or firing themselves from saltheap cannons. Those who survive tend to go to even more extreme lengths to satisfy their thirst for danger.","abilities":["Movement Speed increases briefly when crossing a Rope Bridge or launched by a <Saltheap Cannon>"],"levelCount":1,"level":0,"levelAssumed":false,"statsOverridden":false,"moveSpeed":0.9,"stats":{"hp":6500,"atk":420,"def":60,"res":10,"elementalRes":0,"elementalDamageRes":0,"attackInterval":2}},"explosion_devotee":{"slug":"explosion_devotee","name":"Explosion Devotee","icon":"/enemies-icons/Explosion Devotee.webp","rank":"Elite","race":null,"movement":"Ground","attackPosition":"Ranged","damageType":["Arts"],"flavourText":"The Saltheap Cannon is driven not by Originium explosives, but by the kinetic power of saltfin sinew. Dissatisfied with this state of affairs, some sailors have taken to stuffing massive amounts of improvised powder into metal tubes, trying to light up the night sky of the Salt Flat.","abilities":["Can perform a charged attack, dealing a large amount of Arts Damage to all nearby allied units with a Stun effect","Can ride <Saltfin Breakers>, gaining some of their abilities"],"levelCount":1,"level":0,"levelAssumed":false,"statsOverridden":true,"moveSpeed":0.7,"stats":{"hp":18000,"atk":620,"def":300,"res":50,"elementalRes":0,"elementalDamageRes":0,"attackInterval":2.5}},"bel_canto_boatswain":{"slug":"bel_canto_boatswain","name":"Bel Canto Boatswain","icon":"/enemies-icons/Bel Canto Boatswain.webp","rank":"Elite","race":null,"movement":"Ground","attackPosition":"Melee and Ranged","damageType":["Physical"],"flavourText":"The boatswain's saltfin has caught the sailors' attention, but it does not stop bellowing when the boatswain wants it to. Forced to yell above the saltfin's cacophony, the boatswain has developed a bel canto voice so beautiful that it may impress the salt flat itself.","abilities":["While on the battlefield, <Risk-surviving Sailor> attacks also inflict Corrosion; Periodically summons 2 <Risk-surviving Sailors>","ATK increases when blocked"],"levelCount":1,"level":0,"levelAssumed":false,"statsOverridden":false,"moveSpeed":0.45,"stats":{"hp":30000,"atk":850,"def":800,"res":30,"elementalRes":0,"elementalDamageRes":0,"attackInterval":3}},"saltfin_breaker":{"slug":"saltfin_breaker","name":"Saltfin Breaker","icon":"/enemies-icons/Saltfin Breaker.webp","rank":"Elite","race":null,"movement":"Ground","attackPosition":"Melee","damageType":["Physical"],"flavourText":"Despite its size and weight, this saltfin is surprisingly lithe when swimming through the salts. Normally gentle in nature, it can shatter even hardened ancient salt layers with its powerful slamming attacks when provoked.","abilities":["Attacks deal Physical splash damage to all nearby allied units","Immune to the effects of Salt Flat and gains increased Movement Speed while in Salt Flat"],"levelCount":1,"level":0,"levelAssumed":false,"statsOverridden":false,"moveSpeed":0.3,"stats":{"hp":100000,"atk":2000,"def":0,"res":0,"elementalRes":0,"elementalDamageRes":0,"attackInterval":6}},"terrible_chef":{"slug":"terrible_chef","name":"Terrible Chef","icon":"/enemies-icons/Terrible Chef.webp","rank":"Elite","race":null,"movement":"Ground","attackPosition":"Melee","damageType":["Physical"],"flavourText":"More butcher than cook, the fleet's chefs are more adept at dismembering carcasses than making the aftermath fit for human consumption. No sailor who has seen one dismember a saltfin has the guts to complain about their cooking.","abilities":["More likely to be attacked","Nearby enemies and <Saltheap Cannons> take far less Physical/Arts damage from sources in the direction of the shield"],"levelCount":1,"level":0,"levelAssumed":